[36m(TaskRunner pid=592655)[0m code='\nfrom math import gcd\n\ndef smallest_multiple(n: int) -> int:\n    """\n    Returns the smallest positive integer that is evenly divisible by all integers from 1 to n.\n    \n    Args:\n        n (int): The upper bound of the range (must be a positive integer).\n        \n    Returns:\n        int: The least common multiple (LCM) of all integers from 1 to n.\n        \n    Raises:\n        ValueError: If n is less than 1.\n    """\n    if n < 1:\n        raise ValueError("n must be a positive integer")\n    \n    lcm_value = 1\n    for i in range(1, n + 1):\n        lcm_value = lcm(lcm_value, i)\n    return lcm_value\n\ndef lcm(a: int, b: int) -> int:\n    """\n    Compute the least common multiple of two integers.\n    \n    Args:\n        a (int): First integer.\n        b (int): Second integer.\n        \n    Returns:\n        int: The least common multiple of a and b.\n    """\n    return a * b // gcd(a, b)\n'
